# Context

## Why This Way
The presigned-GET loop (PR #90) hard-coded its transient set and
dropped 408, while every SDK path in s3.rs classifies 408 as
transient via `is_transient_status` (PR #70). The fix aligns both
the retry guard and the final classification so a surviving 408
surfaces as `StoreError::Retryable` — `smart::wal_err` then maps
it to a retryable 503 instead of a permanent 500.

## Gotchas
- The loop's guard cannot call `is_transient_status` directly: it
  also gates on the attempt budget in the same match arm, and the
  set must stay in sync by hand.
- rustfs does not emit 408 on GET, so the contract suite cannot
  cover this; the unit test uses `counting_fake_s3` instead.

## Related
